Introduction to Prometheus

🔹 What is Prometheus? 📊
 Prometheus is an open-source monitoring and alerting tool used to collect and store metrics as time-series data.
 It helps you track system performance in real-time.
👉 “What is happening in my system right now?”

🔹 Why is it used? 🏗️
Modern applications (especially microservices & Kubernetes) need powerful monitoring tools.
👉 Prometheus is used because it:
 ✔ Provides real-time monitoring
 ✔ Works well with dynamic environments
 ✔ Helps detect issues quickly 🚨
🔹 Key Features: ⚡
✔ Pull-based Model 🔄
Prometheus collects metrics by pulling data from targets
✔ Time-Series Database 📈
Stores data with timestamps
Helps track trends over time
✔ Powerful Query Language (PromQL) 🧠
Used to analyze metrics
Create dashboards & alerts
✔ Built-in Alerting Support 🚨
Works with Alertmanager
Sends alerts when conditions are met
✔ Kubernetes Friendly ☸️
Auto-discovers services
Widely used in cloud-native systems

🔹 Real-world Example: 💡
Your application is running on servers
👉 Prometheus collects:
CPU usage
Memory usage
Request count
👉 If CPU > 90% 🚨
 → Alert triggered → Engineers take action

🔹 Key Concepts to Remember: 🧠
✔ Prometheus = Monitoring tool 📊
 ✔ Collects metrics automatically 🔄
 ✔ Stores time-series data 📈
 ✔ Uses PromQL for queries 🧠
 ✔ Helps in alerting 🚨
